    "intro_html":  "Tomato and egg is the first thing a lot of Chinese cooks learn to make, and adding beef turns a quick lunch into an actual dinner. The tomatoes break down into a sweet-sour sauce, the eggs go in soft and silky, and a cornstarch slurry pulls it all together into something glossy that clings to rice. A little ketchup and sugar sounds like cheating and is genuinely how Cantonese restaurants balance the acid. That is a genuinely high protein number for a beef and egg bowl, and eggs are the reason.",
